  {
    "name": "Hunting & Collecting Terrestrial Animals",
    "desc": "Killing/trapping terrestrial wild animals for commercial, subsistence, recreation, research, cultural reasons, or persecution/control; includes accidental mortality. Includes: hunting, trapping, trophy hunting, bushmeat, predator control. Also use when a study describes reintroduction or recovery of a commercially exploited or fur/game species, as prior overexploitation is the implied threat. Semi-aquatic taxa (otters, beavers, amphibians, waterfowl): generally here. Seals, whales, marine mammals, marine turtles: use Fishing & Harvesting Aquatic Resources."
  },
  {
    "name": "Gathering Terrestrial Plants",
    "desc": "Harvesting wild terrestrial plants/fungi: wild mushrooms, medicinal plants, orchid/rattan collection. Boundary: trees/woody vegetation for timber/fibre/fuel use Logging & Wood Harvesting."
  },
  {
    "name": "Logging & Wood Harvesting",
    "desc": "Harvesting trees/woody vegetation from natural/semi-natural systems: clearcutting, selective logging, fuelwood, charcoal, woodchips in quasi-natural forests. Boundary: clearing trees to convert land to agriculture use Agriculture & Aquaculture. Planted timber plantations on rotation use Wood & Pulp Plantations."
  },
  {
    "name": "Fishing & Harvesting Aquatic Resources",
    "desc": "Harvesting wild aquatic animals/plants (freshwater or marine): commercial, subsistence, recreation, persecution/control; includes bycatch. Semi-aquatic distinction: seals, whales, marine mammals, freshwater/marine turtles here; otters/beavers/amphibians/polar bears/penguins/waterfowl/seabirds generally use Hunting & Collecting Terrestrial Animals."
  },
  {
    "name": "Recreational Activities",
    "desc": "Recreation and leisure activities in natural environments without established transport corridors: off-road vehicles, motorboats/jet-skis, snowmobiles, dive boats, hiking, mountain biking, climbing, scuba diving, pets in recreation areas. Boundary: permanent recreation facilities use Tourism & Recreation Areas."
  },
  {
    "name": "War, Civil Unrest & Military Exercises",
    "desc": "Military/paramilitary actions without single permanent facility: armed conflict, training exercises, minefields, military vehicles in field, defoliation, munitions testing. Boundary: permanent military bases use Commercial & Industrial Areas. If soldiers hunt wildlife, code hunting under Hunting & Collecting Terrestrial Animals."
  },
  {
    "name": "Work & Other Activities",
    "desc": "Non-recreational, non-military human presence causing disturbance: research/monitoring, law enforcement patrols, illegal migration routes, vandalism, other work-related intrusions. Boundary: if primarily infrastructure development use Residential & Commercial Development or Transportation & Service Corridors; if primarily consumptive extraction use Biological Resource Use."
  },
  {
    "name": "Roads & Railroads",
    "desc": "Surface transport corridors: highways, secondary roads, logging roads, bridges, railroads; roadkill/wildlife collisions, road-associated fencing. Boundary: off-road vehicles in natural areas not on established road use Recreational Activities. Small roads mainly servicing utility corridors use Utility & Service Lines."
  },
  {
    "name": "Utility & Service Lines",
    "desc": "Linear corridors transporting energy/resources/services: powerlines, pipelines (oil/gas), communication towers; associated wildlife mortality (electrocution). Boundary: if primarily road/rail line with minor utilities, use Roads & Railroads. Oil spills from pipelines: use Industrial & Military Effluents if focus is pollution; use here if corridor itself is emphasised."
  },
  {
    "name": "Shipping Lanes",
    "desc": "Water-based transport corridors and vessel impacts: canals, dredged navigation channels, ship strikes on wildlife (e.g. whale collisions), wake impacts, traffic-related disturbance. Boundary: ports/shipyards as facilities use Commercial & Industrial Areas."
  },
  {
    "name": "Flight Paths",
    "desc": "Air/space transport routes: bird strikes, aircraft overflight disturbance when framed as transport routing. Boundary: airports as built facilities use Commercial & Industrial Areas."
  },
  {
